<title>LEBANON: Star bank shares fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Star bank shares fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The star bank shares on the Beirut Stock Exchange, Banque Libanaise pour le Commerce and Banque Audi, fell on Monday after rising steadily since listing last December and January.</p>
<p>Solidere B shares also fell to $11.75 from $12.25 following a surge last week.</p>
<p>BLC fell to $17 from $17.25 and Banque Audi fell to $20 from $20.125.</p>
<p>BLC has risen from $11.25 since listing on December 30 and Banque Audi has risen from $15 since January 20.</p>
<p>Bank of Beirut was unchanged at $3.5625.</p>
</text>
